---
description: Mandatory UX4G Design System 3.0 rules for all ServiceForm UI work
alwaysApply: false
---
- Read `DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` and `specs/design-system.yaml` before changing UI.
- UX4G Design System 3.0 is the mandatory baseline for Citizen, Officer, Studio, Tenant Admin and platform UI.
- Next.js/React uses UX4G React components/tokens/patterns. Flutter uses UX4G Flutter components/tokens/patterns.
- JSON Forms is schema/runtime only; standard widgets must resolve to UX4G-backed renderers.
- Before creating a control, search UX4G and the ServiceForm extension registry.
- Do not hard-code colors, spacing, typography, radii, shadows or focus states when UX4G tokens exist.
- No MUI/Bootstrap/Tailwind visual design system in product UI without approved ADR + UX4G-conformance wrapper.
- Tenant branding is token overlay only; never tenant CSS/JS/component forks.
- Any custom ServiceForm UX4G extension needs Figma/Storybook parity, accessibility, responsive, localization and visual regression tests.
- Never mark UI VERIFIED without executed test evidence.
